# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two FILES, never a
# shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is defined in run_gates.sh.
# Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
# NOTE: NO backticks and NO dollar-sign in the desc/blurb text below (shell-eval fragility -- see CLAUDE.md).
register_gate "tests/test_g1_head_unresolvable_failclosed.py" "G1 HEAD UNRESOLVABLE FAILCLOSED GATE: PASS" "head-unresolvable withheld-clear (G1 tail): a would-be clear over an UNREADABLE main HEAD is withheld as an honest 'currency not confirmed' Unknown, not falsely emitted as clear" "head-unresolvable withheld-clear silent-miss (G1 tail, a wrong-clear-on-unconfirmable-currency): graph_freshness returns behind=None when main HEAD cannot be resolved from GitHub [head_sha None -- a repo_default_branch_head API failure]. The shipped G1 withhold [_pr_stale_graph_unknown_result] and the shared predicate _graph_degraded DELIBERATELY treat head_sha None as NOT degraded [they return False], so a would-be CLEAR verdict STANDS even though Veripsa cannot confirm the stored code graph is current -- it cannot compare the stored sha to an unknown HEAD. That is a would-be-Clear emitted from an unconfirmable-currency state -> a real overlap whose graph link only exists at the true [unread] HEAD is MISSED -> a SILENT false clear. THE FIX [recall-safe, would-be-Clear ONLY]: when currency cannot be confirmed AND the result would be a clean CLEAR [check conclusion success], withhold it to the honest Unknown -- an advisory neutral 'code graph currency not confirmed -- not cleared' check + comment -- as a SEPARATE, clearly-scoped branch [_graph_head_unresolvable] keyed on self_heal reason 'main HEAD unresolvable' [a genuine API failure; the self-heal-DISABLED return does not match]. _graph_degraded stays UNCHANGED [head_sha None is still NOT degraded] and the behind-and-not-current withhold path is byte-for-byte as-is. Monotonic: this can ONLY turn a would-be Clear into Unknown -- it never suppresses a collision, strips an ACK, or changes a non-success verdict. Content-free, jargon-free, idempotent in-place upsert, never-crash. Drives the REAL handler [server.handle_event] over the REAL gate [db/schema.sql] with a FakeGitHub whose main HEAD is unresolvable [repo_default_branch_head returns an empty head]" "head-unresolvable withheld-clear [G1 tail]: a would-be clear over an UNREADABLE main HEAD is withheld as an advisory 'currency not confirmed' [neutral] and NOT emitted as a false success, while a real collision on the same unresolvable-HEAD event still surfaces [action_required, recall-safe], a resolvable-current HEAD keeps its clear [success, no over-fire], and a resolvable behind-and-not-current graph still triggers the EXISTING G1 stale-graph withhold unchanged -- recall-safe" 20
